meson: drop the PTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK entry from the threads compile_args

On hosts without pthread_condattr_setclock() (macOS) the ternary yields
an empty string, which this meson passes to the compiler verbatim as '', and
gcc then fails with "linker input file not found". Dropping the entry is
safe there, since PTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK could never be defined on such a host
anyway.

See https://github.com/haasn/libplacebo/issues/361

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index dba8fbff..789b0e65 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -510,8 +510,7 @@ else
 
     threads = declare_dependency(
       dependencies: pthreads,
-      compile_args: [pthreads.found() ? '-DPL_HAVE_PTHREAD' : '',
-                     has_setclock ? '-DPTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK' : '',]
+      compile_args: [pthreads.found() ? '-DPL_HAVE_PTHREAD' : '',]
     )
 endif
 
